WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.625
Then the cycle that turns
analysis into delivered change.

2
00:00:03.625 --> 00:00:06.050
Nothing touches the target without a plan,

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:10.000
and no plan touches it without someone
of record having read it first.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.042
Analyze compares the current
state with the target

5
00:00:13.042 --> 00:00:15.588
and produces a diff and
a blast-radius score.

6
00:00:15.588 --> 00:00:20.749
Plan turns the diff into a sequence of
actions, each bounded to a single object,

7
00:00:20.749 --> 00:00:24.378
ordered by dependency and
paired with its own inverse,

8
00:00:24.378 --> 00:00:26.313
so the plan can run backwards.

9
00:00:26.313 --> 00:00:27.537
Then two gates.

10
00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:30.793
Validation rejects any
plan that breaks naming,

11
00:00:30.793 --> 00:00:35.025
scope or safety rules, such as
deleting too many objects at once.

12
00:00:35.025 --> 00:00:37.594
Authorization needs a review and at least

13
00:00:37.594 --> 00:00:40.163
one approver of record
who isn't the author.

14
00:00:40.163 --> 00:00:44.496
Only then does the execution
layer, under a separate identity,

15
00:00:44.496 --> 00:00:48.150
deliver each action, verify
it and record the result.

16
00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:52.962
When something fails, the default is
to halt, and rollback is explicit.

17
00:00:52.962 --> 00:00:55.928
Every run ends in a
signed evidence packet,

18
00:00:55.928 --> 00:01:00.249
and when nothing has drifted, the
next run is a zero-action plan.

19
00:01:00.249 --> 00:01:05.055
A separate rule caps how far
automation may go: record, observe,

20
00:01:05.055 --> 00:01:10.425
advise, gated actuation, and autonomy
only for named low-risk classes.

21
00:01:10.425 --> 00:01:14.065
Tenant-wide role changes,
Conditional Access enforcement

22
00:01:14.065 --> 00:01:17.037
and bulk device changes
stay gated permanently.

23
00:01:17.037 --> 00:01:19.562
No federal document requires that ceiling.

24
00:01:19.562 --> 00:01:23.937
The book chooses it because it's a
posture an authorizing official can sign.

25
00:01:23.937 --> 00:01:26.476
So before the first production delivery,

26
00:01:26.476 --> 00:01:30.805
the authorizing official agrees the
ceiling for each class of change,

27
00:01:30.805 --> 00:01:34.300
with its dry run, its approver
and its rollback on record.
